## Reviewer Report

### 🔴 Critical (must fix before merge)
- `src/engine/resolve-review-loop.js:98` — `assertOneOf(value, 'reviewer_runner', ['codex', 'auto', 'agy', 'grok', 'cc-shim'])` was **not** updated to include `anthropic-compatible`, even though `scripts/resolve-review-loop.sh:239` (this diff) now legitimately emits `"reviewer_runner": "anthropic-compatible"`. `src/engine/autopilot-engine.js:278` wires `resolveReviewLoopJson` (which calls `validateReviewLoopConfig`, `src/engine/resolve-review-loop.js:62-141`) as the **default** review-loop resolver for `AutopilotEngine`. Consequence: any project that sets `reviewer_runner: anthropic-compatible` in `review-loop-config.md` — exactly the config value this diff exists to legitimize — will have the bash resolver succeed but `AutopilotEngine`'s config validation **throw** (`review-loop output JSON field reviewer_runner must be one of: codex, auto, agy, grok, cc-shim`), crashing the engine path that actually drives `/l5`/`/l6` dispatch. The `hooks/tests/contract-parity.test.sh` parity test only checks the template's *default* `reviewer_runner` ("codex"), never exercises the new value, so it silently passes while the real feature is broken downstream. Fix: add `'anthropic-compatible'` to the `assertOneOf` allowlist at `src/engine/resolve-review-loop.js:98`, and add a regression test (either extend `contract-parity.test.sh` to also validate a config forcing `reviewer_runner: anthropic-compatible`, or add a unit assertion directly against `validateReviewLoopConfig`).
- `platforms/codex/plugin/src/engine/resolve-review-loop.js:98` — identical stale enum in the byte-mirrored Codex-plugin copy (verified via `Grep` — only these two JS files plus the two bash scripts contain this literal enum anywhere in the repo). Same fix, same file, mirrored; per `scripts/sync-codex-plugin-skills.sh` this payload is supposed to track the canonical source, so fixing only the canonical file and forgetting the mirror will re-introduce drift the sync `--check` gate should catch — apply both together.

