### Summary
Overall risk: **Medium-High** — the shipped script/doc/test trio is internally consistent and correct, but the change is incomplete: a sibling validation layer (`src/engine/resolve-review-loop.js`, consumed by `AutopilotEngine`, the actual `/l5`/`/l6` dispatch engine) still hard-rejects the exact new value this diff introduces, in both the canonical and Codex-plugin-mirrored copies. Left as-is, the feature "works" only when accessed via the raw bash script / `--field` CLI, and throws when accessed through the JS engine path that project docs describe as the live dispatch mechanism.

Top 3 priorities to fix:
1. Add `'anthropic-compatible'` to `assertOneOf(value, 'reviewer_runner', …)` in `src/engine/resolve-review-loop.js:98` (canonical).
2. Apply the identical fix to `platforms/codex/plugin/src/engine/resolve-review-loop.js:98` (mirror) in the same commit.
3. Extend `hooks/tests/contract-parity.test.sh` (or add a new assertion) to exercise `reviewer_runner: anthropic-compatible` through `validateReviewLoopConfig`, so this class of drift is caught mechanically instead of requiring a manual cross-file `Grep` sweep next time.

